# Current packages

Before adding a dependency, confirm the registry does not mark it deprecated and that it still receives releases. Do not add a package that only exists to keep an abandoned API compiling.

Do not add new imports of packages already in the repo that are deprecated or maintenance-only:

- `aws-sdk` (v2). New AWS calls use `@aws-sdk/client-*`.
- `moment`. New date code uses built-in `Date` and `Intl`, unless a maintained date library is already installed in that package.

When a change touches a file that imports one of those, new code in that file uses the successor. Do not start a repo-wide upgrade unless asked.

```ts
// do not add
import AWS from "aws-sdk";
import moment from "moment";

// add this instead
import { DynamoDBClient } from "@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb";
const label = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-ZA").format(new Date());
```
